   "name": "sty_mint_a0",
   "comment": "MINT an ObjStyle where >= 3 of ONE source's projected items agree EXACTLY on AXIS 0's within-category offset (dv0). THE STYLE IS A DISCOVERED DIMENSION: there is ONE RULE PER AXIS and BOTH run on EVERY source, so nothing tells the mechanism which axis carries the style -- a source whose axis-0 offsets cohere while its other axis varies freely mints EXACTLY ONE style, on axis 0, and the minted node RECORDS the axis it found. A source that coheres on neither mints NOTHING (the coherence crux: a mechanism that mints a style for ANY source would be a universal container and is disqualified). This is the Omniglot writer-dimension mint one level up (writer_dimensions.json:228 -- pool per source, require >= 3 exact agreement, mint the implied dimension); per-instance an offset is noise, POOLED across one source's output it is a coherent quantum coordinate. MDL: m_min = 3 FALLS OUT of d_style = 2 -- a style is an (axis, delta) PAIR (2 units: WHICH axis + WHAT offset) and membership is FREE because the source is OBSERVED (the produced edge), so the style pays iff m > d_style = 2 <=> m >= 3 (VISION_PROTOCOL sec 13; NOT tuned, and the same >= 3 the writer rung derived). Guards: (a) the CANONICAL-REPRESENTATIVE guard -- only the min-oidx member of an agreeing pool may mint, so under batch tick() (all bindings snapshotted before any effect) exactly ONE member mints exactly ONE style per (source, axis, delta); (b) Not Exists an ObjStyle already at this (src, axis, delta) -- recognize-not-re-mint across passes. Records src / axis / delta / members and the minting instance's RAW exemplar (ex_v0, ex_v1) for the memorization control. UNSUPERVISED: no label is read; the SOURCE is an observable (which hand produced it), not a category label. Flag-gated on style>0.5, OFF by default (sec 9).",
